From: Alexander Grucza <a.grucza@gmx.net>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: axp20x_battery: report "full" once the charger has terminated

The status property trusts the battery current direction bit in
PWR_INPUT_STATUS (bit 2) alone: whenever current flows into the battery
the status is reported as charging. On an AXP228 that bit stays set after
the charger has terminated, because a residual current of about 1 mA keeps
flowing into the cell, so userspace sees "Charging" indefinitely and the
"Full" branch, which additionally needs the fuel gauge to read exactly
100 %, is never reached.

PWR_OP_MODE bit 6 is the charger's own indication, documented as "1: in
charging, 0: not charging or charge finished" for the AXP20x/22x/8xx
family. Consult it when the direction bit says "charging": if the charger
has finished, report the battery as full. Keep reporting "charging" while
the chip is in battery activation mode (PWR_OP_MODE bit 3), where a small
current flows into a deeply discharged cell without the charging flag set.

Observed on a ClockworkPi uConsole with an AXP228: at the end of a charge
PWR_INPUT_STATUS read 0xc4 (bit 2 set) with current_now at 1000 uA and the
battery resting at 4.17 V, while PWR_OP_MODE read 0x30 (bit 6 clear) and
the CHGLED, once handed to the charger, had gone out. With this change the
status property reports "Full" in that state.

Signed-off-by: Alexander Grucza <a.grucza@gmx.net>
---
 drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/axp20x_battery.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 #define AXP717_PWR_STATUS_BAT_CHRG	1
 #define AXP717_PWR_STATUS_BAT_DISCHRG	2
 
+#define AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_CHARGING	BIT(6)
 #define AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_PRESENT	BIT(5)
 #define AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_ACTIVATED	BIT(3)
 #define AXP717_PWR_OP_BATT_PRESENT	BIT(3)
@@ -298,7 +299,29 @@
 			return ret;
 
 		if (reg & AXP20X_PWR_STATUS_BAT_CHARGING) {
-			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			/*
+			 * This bit only reports the direction of the battery
+			 * current. After the charger has terminated, a residual
+			 * current of a few mA keeps flowing into the battery, so
+			 * the bit stays set and the status would read "charging"
+			 * forever. The charger's own "in charging" flag in
+			 * PWR_OP_MODE tells whether a charge is really going on;
+			 * when it is clear with current still flowing in, the
+			 * charge has finished, unless the chip is trickling a
+			 * deeply discharged cell in activation mode.
+			 */
+			ret = regmap_read(axp20x_batt->regmap,
+					  AXP20X_PWR_OP_MODE, &val1);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+
+			if (val1 & AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_CHARGING)
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			else if (val1 & AXP20X_PWR_OP_BATT_ACTIVATED)
+				/* activation trickle into a deeply discharged cell */
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+			else
+				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 			return 0;
 		}
 
